%N A399601 Number of nonisomorphic rectangular ideal extensions of order n of left zero (trivial) doppelsemigroups by null quotients.
%C A399601 Also, a(n) is the number of nonisomorphic rectangular ideal extensions of order n of right zero (trivial) doppelsemigroups by null quotients.
%C A399601 Also, a(n) is the number of nonisomorphic inflations of order n of left zero (trivial) doppelsemigroups, in which the two retractions agree on the image but may differ outside it.
%C A399601 Also, a(n) is the number of nonisomorphic inflations of order n of right zero (trivial) doppelsemigroups, in which the two retractions agree on the image but may differ outside it.
%C A399601 A doppelsemigroup is an algebraic structure (D,-|,|-) consisting of a set D equipped with two associative binary operations -| and |- satisfying the following axioms:
%C A399601    (x -| y) |- z = x -| (y |- z),
%C A399601    (x |- y) -| z = x |- (y -| z).
%C A399601 A doppelsemigroup (D,-|,|-) is called rectangular if both (D,-|) and (D,|-) are rectangular semigroups in the sense that
%C A399601    x -| y -| z = x -| z and x |- y |- z = x |- z
%C A399601 for all x,y,z from D.
%C A399601 A doppelsemigroup (D,-|,|-) with -| = |- is called trivial.
%H A399601 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="/A399601/b399601.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..110</a>
